! A Bloom filter is a memory-efficient Set-like data structure. Being an
! example of a probabilistic data structure, Bloom filters can give a
! false positive result when testing for membership.
! 
! Task
! 
! Implement a Bloom filter with membership and add operations. Demonstrate
! that your implementation is more memory-efficient than an equivalent Set
! that stores a hash for each element.
! 
! Other set operations such as union, intersection and difference are
! optional. A counting Bloom filter supporting a delete operation is
! probably best left for another task.


